course: dictionary
lesson: 13277
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning the writer wants by reading the words around it, which is its context. The noun gout has two meanings: a painful illness, and a spurt or drop of liquid in older writing.
explain: «Grandad could not walk to the shop because his big toe was swollen and red with gout.» The clues are swollen, red and could not walk, so gout must be an illness that hurts. Check by swapping in your meaning: an illness fits the sentence, and a drop of liquid does not.
explain: «Gouts of blood ran down the knight's arm.» Here there is no illness at all. Gouts of blood are spurts or drops, so the writer means the second meaning. Older stories often use it this way, to paint a picture with words.
fact: Gout is a noun, which means it names a thing.
fact: Gout is a painful illness that makes joints, especially the big toe, swollen, red and sore.
fact: In history, gout was linked to rich food and drink, and King Henry VIII suffered from it.
fact: «Gouts» in older stories means spurts or drops of liquid, such as «gouts of blood» or «gouts of water».
fact: When a word has two meanings, the context tells you which meaning to use.
exercise: «Her big toe was swollen and sore with gout.» What is gout here? | A spurt of liquid | A type of cake | *A painful illness | A kind of shoe
exercise: «Gouts of water burst from the broken pipe.» What does gouts mean here? | Sad, grey clouds | Loud bangs | *Quick spurts or drops of liquid | Long, cold winters
exercise: In history, which king is said to have suffered from gout? | King Alfred | *King Henry VIII | King Arthur | King Canute
test: «Grandad said his gout made every step hurt.» What does gout mean here? | *A painful illness that swells the joints | A drop of liquid | A tiny insect | A type of fruit
test: «Gouts of flame lit up the dark sky.» What does gouts mean here? | *Spurts or bursts | Clouds | Stars | Shadows
exam: Which sentence uses gout to mean an illness? | «Gouts of paint splashed the wall.» | *«Her swollen knee and sore toe were signs of gout.» | «Gouts of rain fell from the sky.» | «The gouts of the tap dripped all night.»
